<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38815" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπηλῠγ-άζω</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπηλῠγ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>overshadow, cover,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰς ἱματίοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					4.7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				3.16
			</span></i>, al.:—
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ κοινῷ φόβῳ τὸν σφέτερον
				ἐπηλυγάζεσθαι</span>
			<i>throw a shade over,</i> i.e. <i>disguise, conceal</i> one's
				<i>own</i> fear by . ., <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.36
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τὴν χεῖρα</span>
			<i>hold one's</i> hand <i>as a shade over one's eyes,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				780b19
			</span></i>; and (without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χεῖρα</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ἐ. πρὸ τῶν
			ὀμμάτων</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				781b12
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aristocl.
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				14.18
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπηλυγισάμενός τινα</span>
			<i>putting</i> him <i>as a screen before one,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ly.</u>
				207b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ὕλην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					559a1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				613b9
			</span></i>; <i>use as a lurking place,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπήν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				623a29
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be concealed,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τῆς ἀγνωσίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				29
			</span></i>; <i>to be suppressed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				2.156
			</span></i>. (Both <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-άζω</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίζω</span> are found in codd.)</div>
